{"run_name": "toolcall_mod_veerman_minimax-m2.5_20260703_222903", "suite": "veerman", "model": "minimax-m2.5", "model_slug": "minimax-m2.5", "case_id": "veerman_p4_ambiguous_brussels", "category": "veerman_action", "split": "veerman", "prompt": "I'm heading to Brussels tomorrow, anything I should know?", "expected_tools": [{"name": "get_weather_v", "args": {"city": "Brussels"}}], "multi_turn": false, "timestamp": "2026-07-03T22:29:47.877314", "turn_1_elapsed_s": 6.423, "turn_1_tool_calls": [], "turn_1_text": "\n\nBrussels is a wonderful city to visit! Here are some things you should know:\n\n**Weather**: Brussels has a temperate maritime climate. In July, expect mild weather with temperatures around 15-25°C (59-77°F). Pack layers and a light jacket for rain.\n\n**Language**: Brussels is bilingual (Dutch/French), but English is widely spoken in tourist areas.\n\n**Currency**: Belgium uses the Euro (€).\n\n**Must-see spots**:\n- Grand Place (Grote Markt) – stunning medieval square\n- Manneken Pis – the famous peeing boy statue\n- Atomium – iconic 1958 structure\n- European Parliament buildings\n- Museums like the Magritte Museum or Royal Museums of Fine Arts\n\n**Food & Drink**: Don't miss Belgian waffles, fries (mayonnaise!), mussels, and of course, chocolate! And sample some of the many local beers.\n\n**Transport**: The city has an efficient metro, tram, and bus network. You can get a Brussels Card for unlimited public transport and museum discounts.\n\nIs there anything specific you'd like more information on, or would you like me to check the weather forecast for Brussels?", "turn_1_finish_reason": "stop", "prompt_tokens": 451, "completion_tokens": 278, "total_tokens": 729, "tok_s": 43.28, "engine_generation_tps": null, "engine_prompt_tps": null, "engine_peak_memory_gb": null, "turn_2_elapsed_s": null, "turn_2_tool_calls": null, "turn_2_text": null, "turn_2_usage": null, "score_pass": false, "score_reason": "no_tool_called", "score_breakdown": {"tool_called": fal